Summary: Kick the habit


Often, you'll be better off kicking ants and other 'a's than using your weapon.
(Especially if you are a priest or a samurai.)
Don't forget that a dagger has a +1 to hit, and ants etc. never have that
many hit points (the trick is hitting them in the first place) so sometimes
a dagger is your best choice especially if your main weapon is +0.
Sometimes in a running battle against ants, I leave 'Elbereth' inscribed
all over the level.  Use your finger if you don't have an athame or wand
suitable for inscribing.
Quite often, they kill me.  I think possibly soldier ants are really too hard
for the 1st ten levels.  In any case, perhaps they should be implemented as
weaker monsters but a deal more of them, sheer numbers being the usual strong
point of ants.
Weaker character types really do have to keep their dog around until level
10 or so.
I think a flyswatter woudl be a cool weapon (appliance?) ...  make it 1d1
or 1d2 at the most in damage, but +4 to hit against 'a's.  Give the tourist
a flyswatter; his pack is already loaded with anachronisms anyhow.

